WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.477
Validation tests values against documented rules.

00:00:03.477 --> 00:00:09.792
A rule might describe a text pattern, a length, a domain, or a numeric range.

00:00:09.792 --> 00:00:13.502
Passing a rule means the value satisfies that rule.

00:00:13.502 --> 00:00:17.797
It does not necessarily prove the value is correct in the real world.

00:00:17.797 --> 00:00:22.687
Keep the distinction between validity and accuracy from Module 1.

00:00:22.687 --> 00:00:28.752
Connect this idea to a customer master-data project cleaning duplicate profiles.

00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:34.422
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:34.422 --> 00:00:42.232
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:42.232 --> 00:00:47.917
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:47.917 --> 00:00:53.760
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
